{"seq":1,"slug":"embedding-geometry","title":"嵌入空间几何：对齐与均匀，一对好空间的判据","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/metric-learning-embeddings/geometry/embedding-geometry","wordCount":1475,"readingTime":6,"html":"<h1 id=\"嵌入空间几何-对齐与均匀-一对好空间的判据\">嵌入空间几何：对齐与均匀，一对好空间的判据</h1><p>同样一个 Recall@K 数字，背后的嵌入空间可能截然不同：一个把每个类别压成紧致的小簇、均匀铺满超球面；另一个所有向量挤在一个窄锥里、靠微小的角度差勉强区分。前者稳健、后者脆弱。问题是——训练损失曲线看不出这种差别。本篇引入一套<strong>直接刻画空间形状</strong>的视角，其中最有影响力的是 Wang 与 Isola（2020）提出的&quot;对齐性—均匀性&quot;这对可量化判据。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念-超球面上的两个理想\">核心概念：超球面上的两个理想</h2><p>L2 归一化后，所有嵌入住在单位超球面 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 上。一个理想的度量空间应同时满足两点：<strong>对齐性</strong>（alignment）——正样本对应当彼此贴近；<strong>均匀性</strong>（uniformity）——所有样本应尽量均匀地摊开、充分利用整个球面。这两者是一对张力：只求对齐会坍缩（大家挤成一团也&quot;对齐&quot;），只求均匀会散掉正样本。好的损失是在两者间找平衡。Wang-Isola 给出了可计算的度量：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L</mi><mtext>align</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L</mi><mtext>unif</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{align}} = \\mathbb{E}_{(x,x^+)}\\lVert f(x)-f(x^+)\\rVert^2, \\quad \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{unif}} = \\log\\, \\mathbb{E}_{x,y}\\, e^{-t\\lVert f(x)-f(y)\\rVert^2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">align</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1052em;vertical-align:-0.3552em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5198em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7027em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.786em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3552em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1141em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8213em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">∥</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:1em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">unif</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.323em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0369em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\"><span class=\"mclose mtight\">∥</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p>对齐损失越小说明正对越贴近；均匀损失越小说明点在球面上越接近均匀分布（对应高斯势能最小）。他们证明 InfoNCE 在极限下恰好同时优化这两项——这解释了对比损失为何有效。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>性质</th>\n<th>理想状态</th>\n<th>度量</th>\n<th>崩坏表现</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>对齐性</td>\n<td>正对贴近</td>\n<td><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{E}\\lVert f(x)-f(x^+)\\rVert^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">E</span><span class=\"mopen\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">∥</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 小</td>\n<td>类内散开，召回低</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>均匀性</td>\n<td>均匀铺满球面</td>\n<td>高斯势能低</td>\n<td>各向异性/锥效应</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>平衡</td>\n<td>紧簇+摊开</td>\n<td>两者兼低</td>\n<td>坍缩或散乱</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart TD&#10;    A[L2 归一化嵌入&lt;br/&gt;住在单位超球面] --&gt; B[对齐性 alignment]&#10;    A --&gt; C[均匀性 uniformity]&#10;    B --&gt; D[正样本对彼此贴近]&#10;    C --&gt; E[所有点均匀铺满球面]&#10;    D --&gt; F{两者平衡}&#10;    E --&gt; F&#10;    F --&gt;|只求对齐| G[坍缩: 挤成一团]&#10;    F --&gt;|只求均匀| H[散乱: 正对被拆开]&#10;    F --&gt;|兼得| I[理想: 紧致小簇 + 充分展开]\">flowchart TD\n    A[L2 归一化嵌入&lt;br/&gt;住在单位超球面] --&gt; B[对齐性 alignment]\n    A --&gt; C[均匀性 uniformity]\n    B --&gt; D[正样本对彼此贴近]\n    C --&gt; E[所有点均匀铺满球面]\n    D --&gt; F{两者平衡}\n    E --&gt; F\n    F --&gt;|只求对齐| G[坍缩: 挤成一团]\n    F --&gt;|只求均匀| H[散乱: 正对被拆开]\n    F --&gt;|兼得| I[理想: 紧致小簇 + 充分展开]</pre><h2 id=\"各向异性与锥效应-看不见的空间病\">各向异性与锥效应：看不见的空间病</h2><p>一个在 NLP 嵌入里被反复观察到的病灶是<strong>各向异性</strong>（anisotropy）：向量并非均匀分布在球面上，而是集中在一个狭窄的锥形区域里，导致任意两个向量的余弦相似度都偏高、彼此难以区分——这被称为&quot;锥效应&quot;。BERT 未经处理的句向量就有严重各向异性，直接拿来算相似度效果很差。根因是频率等因素让表示退化到低维主方向。对策包括白化（whitening）、后处理去除主成分、或在训练时显式加均匀性正则。均匀性差是各向异性的本质，而各向异性又与低秩、维度坍缩紧密相连，后者专门在 <a href=\"dimensionality-collapse\">维度坍缩</a>展开。</p>\n<p>诊断各向异性有个简单办法：随机采一批向量，算它们两两余弦相似度的均值——理想均匀分布下应接近 0，若显著大于 0 就说明空间被挤进了锥里。</p>\n<h2 id=\"曲率的选择-欧氏球面之外还有双曲空间\">曲率的选择：欧氏球面之外还有双曲空间</h2><p>默认大家都在&quot;平&quot;的欧氏空间（归一化后即球面）里嵌入，但空间的曲率本身也是可选的。对于<strong>层级结构</strong>数据（分类树、词的上下位关系、社交网络），双曲空间（hyperbolic，负曲率）有天然优势：双曲空间的体积随半径指数增长，恰好匹配树的分支指数增长，能用很低的维度无失真地嵌入一棵深树。Poincaré 嵌入就是把词汇的 is-a 层级放进双曲球，用极少维度捕捉层级。代价是双曲空间的距离、优化都更复杂，工程门槛高。绝大多数检索任务仍用欧氏/球面就够，但当数据本质是层级时，曲率是一个值得考虑的旋钮。这种&quot;用几何结构匹配数据结构&quot;的思路，与 <a href=\"../../dimensionality-reduction/foundations/linear-vs-nonlinear\">降维</a>里线性与非线性流形的取舍相通。</p>\n<h2 id=\"几何如何指导损失与调参\">几何如何指导损失与调参</h2><p>理解几何不是为了美学，而是为了诊断和干预。若发现类内散、召回低——对齐不足，该加强正样本约束或减小间隔。若发现相似度普遍偏高、区分度差——均匀性不足/各向异性，该加均匀性正则或白化后处理。若发现空间维度实际很低（有效秩远小于 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span></span></span></span></span>）——正在坍缩，见下一节的对策。这些干预的具体旋钮，很大一部分落在归一化与温度上：温度直接影响均匀性的强度，见 <a href=\"normalization-temperature\">归一化与温度</a>。而空间好不好的最终裁判，仍是检索指标 <a href=\"../practice/evaluation-metrics\">评估 (Recall@K)</a>——几何是解释，指标是判决。</p>\n<p>症状与干预可对照成一张诊断表：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>观察到的症状</th>\n<th>对应几何问题</th>\n<th>干预手段</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>类内散、Recall@K 低</td>\n<td>对齐不足</td>\n<td>加强正样本约束 / 减小间隔</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>相似度普遍偏高、区分差</td>\n<td>均匀性差/各向异性</td>\n<td>均匀性正则 / 白化后处理</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>有效秩远小于 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n<td>正在坍缩</td>\n<td>去相关、方差下界（见坍缩篇）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>层级数据检索失真</td>\n<td>欧氏曲率不匹配</td>\n<td>尝试双曲空间嵌入</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>L2 归一化把嵌入放上单位超球面；好空间需同时满足对齐性（正对贴近）与均匀性（铺满球面）。</li>\n<li>二者是一对张力，Wang-Isola 给出可计算度量，并证明 InfoNCE 在极限下同时优化两者。</li>\n<li>各向异性/锥效应是均匀性差的表现，NLP 句向量常见，可用白化或均匀性正则缓解。</li>\n<li>曲率也是旋钮：层级数据可用双曲空间低维无失真嵌入；几何用于诊断损失与调参，指标是最终判决。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"延伸阅读\">延伸阅读</h3><ul>\n<li>同 hub：<a href=\"normalization-temperature\">归一化与温度</a> — 均匀性的直接旋钮</li>\n<li>同 hub：<a href=\"dimensionality-collapse\">维度坍缩</a> — 对齐过头的失败模式</li>\n<li>跨 hub：<a href=\"../../dimensionality-reduction/foundations/linear-vs-nonlinear\">降维 · 线性与非线性</a> — 流形与曲率的姊妹讨论</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"嵌入空间几何：对齐与均匀，一对好空间的判据","id":"嵌入空间几何-对齐与均匀-一对好空间的判据"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念：超球面上的两个理想","id":"核心概念-超球面上的两个理想"},{"level":2,"text":"各向异性与锥效应：看不见的空间病","id":"各向异性与锥效应-看不见的空间病"},{"level":2,"text":"曲率的选择：欧氏球面之外还有双曲空间","id":"曲率的选择-欧氏球面之外还有双曲空间"},{"level":2,"text":"几何如何指导损失与调参","id":"几何如何指导损失与调参"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"},{"level":3,"text":"延伸阅读","id":"延伸阅读"}],"prev":{"title":"基于代理的损失：让类代理终结采样噩梦","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/metric-learning-embeddings/losses/proxy-based"},"next":{"title":"归一化与温度：两个旋钮，决定梯度的脾气","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/metric-learning-embeddings/geometry/normalization-temperature"}}